# Backend configuration. Copy to `.env` for your own notes, but see the warning
# below — unlike the frontend, this file is NOT loaded automatically.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every variable here has a working development default, so the server runs with
# nothing set at all.

# Origins allowed to call this API from a browser, comma-separated, no spaces.
# Default: http://localhost:5173 (the Vite dev server).
#
# Set this to your deployed frontend's origin in production. An origin is scheme
# + host + port, with no trailing slash or path.
#
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://ctgmap.example,http://localhost:5173
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# --- Note: this file is documentation, not configuration --------------------
#
# The frontend's .env is read automatically because Vite does that. Python does
# not, and no dotenv loader is installed here, so the server reads these from the
# real environment. Set them in your shell before starting uvicorn:
#
#   macOS/Linux:  export ALLOWED_ORIGINS="http://localhost:5173"
#   PowerShell:   $env:ALLOWED_ORIGINS = "http://localhost:5173"
#
# If you would rather load this file directly, `pip install python-dotenv` and
# start with `uvicorn app.main:app --env-file .env`.
